title: Withdraw indictment
subtitle: With the liberals keeping this government alive, is this the right move?
on-arrival: select_committee_called = 1; old_middle_labour -= 10; new_middle_labour -= 10; workers_labour += 3; unemployed_labour -= 8; rural_labour -= 5; tories_relation -= 15; liberals_relation -= 15;

Fearing rebellion from more left leaning backbenchers. MacDonald reluctantly gets Hastings to withdraw his indictment. Prompting widespread fears this government is under soviet influence. The MP for Glasgow Hillhead, Robert Horne calls a resolution to censure the government. Failing 198 - 359. But this will not be the end of this it seems. 

